# What never belongs in the repository -- and, via tools/backup.sh, never in a backup either.
#
# One list, two consumers. Keeping them separate is how a backup ends up carrying a stale
# .ruff_cache that a `git status` would never have shown.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- build and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- environments
.venv/
venv/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- editors, desktops
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- this project
#
# Vendor data is never redistributed: Jabra's property catalogue is fetched from GN Audio's own
# publication on consent, and Poly's catalogues are unpacked from the user's own installer. Both
# land in the user's data directory rather than here, but a stray copy dropped in the tree for
# testing must not be committed by accident.
properties.json
DeviceSettings.zip
*.msi
*.asar

# Backups live beside the checkout, not inside it -- but guard against a stray one anyway.
hardware-ui-backup-*.tar.gz

# `hardware_ui/third_party/` is deliberately NOT ignored. Solaar's subset is vendored on purpose,
# with its licence, copyright and provenance, and is regenerated by tools/vendor_solaar.py.
# See docs/LOGITECH_UI_BEHAVIOUR.md §1.
